# Down in the Valley, strum along (repertoire plan: down-in-the-valley). Your part: a waltz
# strum in 3/4 with two chords, A (x02220) and E7 (020100): the bass note alone on beat 1 (open
# string 5 under A, open string 6 under E7), downstrums on beats 2 and 3.
# Each sung line takes four bars, two per chord: A for "Down in the valley", E7 for "valley so
# low" and "hang your head over", A for "hear the wind blow". The words are written above the
# bar where each chord starts, as on a chord sheet; the learner sings the tune. The tune itself is
# not written out here: it is traditional with many variants, and this arrangement gives only the
# accompaniment the plan specifies. Two traditional verses; the "Birmingham Jail" verses (and
# "Write me a letter", which names the jail) are left out on purpose.
title: Down in the Valley
id: down-in-the-valley
composer: Traditional American
source: Traditional American song, collected by 1909; accompaniment arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: strumming, waltz, 3/4, two chords
tempo: 108
time: 3/4
key: A

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
